     <item>
      <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox_2">
       <property name="whatsThis">
        <string>&lt;p&gt;These don't directly control the actor's skill values. Rather, they act as proportions. For example, if a particular skill has a weight of N, the base value of that skill (determined by game settings and the actor's racial bonuses) is B, the total weight of all skills is S, and an actor has P total skill points to distribute, then that particular skill's final value will be (N&amp;nbsp;÷&amp;nbsp;S)&amp;nbsp;×&amp;nbsp;P&amp;nbsp;+&amp;nbsp;B.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The number of total skill points to distribute is the actor's level, minus one, times the value of the iAVDskillsLevelUp game setting. Those skill points are divided across the actor's skills per their class's skill weights; and then afterward, each skill is increased by the value of the iAVDSkillStart game setting, and then further increased by however bonus points their Race grants to each given skill.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
       </property>
       <property name="title">
        <string>Skill weights</string>
       </property>
